    "summary": "High‑energy Brent era with soaring Bird Song and a smoking Scarlet>Fire",
    "blurb": "The St. Paul show delivers a blistering first set highlighted by Bird Song and Lazy Lightning > Supplication, then erupts in the second set with a classic Scarlet Begonias > Fire on the Mountain and tight Lost Sailor > Saint Of Circumstance jams. Jerry’s lead work is on fire, Brent’s keyboards are full‑bodied, and the rhythm section drives the band forward throughout.",
    "review": "What unfolds at the St. Paul Civic Center captures the Dead in prime Brent‑era form. The first set opens strong with a crisp Bertha that slides into New Minglewood Blues before the band settles into a gorgeous Bird Song; the Lazy Lightning > Supplication pairing showcases Jerry’s searing leads and Brent’s lush organ textures, setting an electric tone for the night. In the second set the band locks in on Scarlet Begonias > Fire on the Mountain – a soaring, high‑octane sequence that many fans cite as one of the era’s finest – then rides a flowing Lost Sailor > Saint Of Circumstance groove into an expansive jam, space, and drums. The rhythm section stays tight, with Mickey and Bill providing propulsive beats while Phil’s bass underpins every improvisational turn, even if it sits a touch low in some mixes. Overall the performance is a vivid snapshot of 1982: high‑energy, richly textured, and brimming with memorable moments that reward repeated listening.",
